The changes I made:
1. Added required properties to the app object:
   - `slug`: Required for links and identification
   - `categories`: Array of categories (required by AppCard)
   - `enabled`: Boolean flag for app state
   - `isInstalled`: Boolean flag indicating installation status
   - `isSetupAlready`: Boolean flag indicating setup status
2. Kept all other functionality the same

These changes should resolve the TypeError by providing all the required properties that the AppCard component expects. The error was occurring because the component was trying to access properties that didn't exist in our mock app object.

